<article class="env-lemma" id="0BYK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BYK">Lemma <span data-tag="0BYK">15.61.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a ring map. Let $f : L^\bullet \to N^\bullet $ be a map of complexes of $A$-modules. Then $f$ induces a transformation of functors </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  1 \otimes f : - \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} L^\bullet \longrightarrow - \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} N^\bullet  \]
</div>
  <p> If $f$ is a quasi-isomorphism, then $1 \otimes f$ is an isomorphism of functors. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since the functors are computing by evaluating on K-flat complexes $K^\bullet $ we can simply use the functoriality 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Tot}(K^\bullet \otimes _ R L^\bullet ) \to \text{Tot}(K^\bullet \otimes _ R N^\bullet )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       to define the transformation. The last statement follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/06Y0" data-tag="06Y0">15.60.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>